THIRD-PARTY NOTICES AND PROVENANCE
===================================

kokoro.cpp — standalone CPU inference for Kokoro-82M TTS

Provenance
----------

The inference code in this project is derived from CrispASR
(https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispASR), which implements the Kokoro
TTS runtime among many other speech models. The extraction is based on
CrispASR commit ef33e2e2ffb567528f082b142a7db69abee94ce0.

  - Preserves inference-critical math (forward pass graphs, GGUF tensor
    naming, tokenizer, iSTFT, and SineGen).
  - Removes GPU backends, multi-model orchestration, and non-Kokoro paths.
  - Renames symbols from CRISPASR_*/crispasr_* to KOKORO_*/kokoro_*.
  - Simplifies to require espeak-ng as a direct linked dependency.

ggml (submodule)
----------------

  Source: https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml
  License: MIT

  The ggml tensor library provides the compute backend for all neural
  network operations (conv, matmul, LSTM gates, attention).

Google Highway (submodule)
--------------------------

  Source: https://github.com/google/highway
  License: Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause, at the user's choice

  Highway provides runtime-dispatched portable SIMD math for harmonic-source
  sine generation, Gaussian noise, and the 20-point STFT. Its vector random
  helper is separately dedicated to the public domain under CC0-1.0. Full
  license texts are retained in `highway/LICENSE`.

espeak-ng (linked dependency)
-----------------------------

  Source: https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
  License: GPLv3+

  espeak-ng is used for text-to-phoneme conversion. A default build
  (KOKORO_ESPEAK=ON) links espeak-ng directly into the resulting binary
  (not loaded at runtime via dlopen).

  IMPORTANT: Because espeak-ng is licensed under GPLv3+, any binary that
  links this library (including the kokoro static library and the
  kokoro-cli tool) is subject to the terms of the GNU General Public
  License version 3 or later. This means:

    1. The combined work must be distributed under GPLv3+ terms.
    2. Complete corresponding source code must be made available.
    3. Users must receive a copy of the GPL license.

  A build configured with -DKOKORO_ESPEAK=OFF does not link espeak-ng.
  It accepts IPA phonemes through kokoro_synthesize_phonemes() and
  kokoro_synthesize_phonemes_audio(); text input returns an error.

  The kokoro library code itself (src/kokoro.cpp, src/phoneme_utils.h,
  include/kokoro.h, etc.) is MIT-licensed. Only the act of linking with
  espeak-ng creates GPL obligations on the combined binary.

